From 9c14f76eb8002ba92f87bea9df8af90749707533 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev <dev@local>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 09:23:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] feat(device-library): list and stream the phone's own
 music collection

The shell can read MediaStore for the user's audio and stream each track from
its original content:// item with full Range support, so a phone library of
thousands of tracks costs no disk, no OPFS quota and no import wait.

- deviceAudioLibrary: probes window.foliaAndroid, asks for READ_MEDIA_AUDIO,
  reads /api/device-audio and builds the stream / album-art URLs.
- deviceAudioSync: merges the collection into local_music as ordinary
  LocalSong rows, so the existing folder / album / artist grouping, lyric
  matching and playlist code work on these songs unchanged. Re-syncing keeps
  every user-produced field and only refreshes MediaStore's own ones; a
  granted-but-empty read is refused rather than treated as "all music gone".
- getAudioFromLocalSong routes a device song to its stream URL; the File and
  ArrayBuffer readers return null for one instead of downloading it whole.
- The local tab's refresh action re-reads the collection, which is also where
  the permission dialog is raised from a real click.
